# News API Integration Plan

The goal is to fetch news from an API and display them in the [NewsSection](file:///c:/Users/USUARIO/Desktop/pruebas/components/NewsSection.tsx#3-20) component, adapting the data to fit the existing UI "boxes".

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I need the **API Endpoint** and **API Key** (if required) to implement the actual fetching. For now, I will implement a flexible structure where you can easily plug in these details.
> If you have the specific API details (e.g., RapidAPI URL), please provide them.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. API Service
#### [NEW] [lib/api.ts](file:///c:/Users/USUARIO/Desktop/pruebas/lib/api.ts)
- Create a function `fetchNews()` that makes the HTTP request.
- Define a `NewsArticle` interface to type the data.
- **Note**: I will use a placeholder URL or a mock if the real one isn't provided.

### 2. UI Updates
#### [MODIFY] [components/NewsSection.tsx](file:///c:/Users/USUARIO/Desktop/pruebas/components/NewsSection.tsx)
- Add state for `news` and `loading`.
- Use `useEffect` to call `fetchNews()` on mount.
- Map the fetched data to the UI cards.
- Handle loading and error states.

### 3. Component Adaptation
- Ensure the API data fields (e.g., `title`, `description`, `image`, `url`) are correctly mapped to the component's props.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Verify that the application compiles.

### Manual Verification
- Check if the news section displays the fetched data (or mock data) correctly.
- Verify responsiveness and layout.
